    "rich_text_q7D8ce": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "spacer_DyTCUA": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 40
          }
        },
        "heading_MrGjAB": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Taper Candles FAQs: Your Questions Answered",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "heading_font_class": "fs-heading-3-base"
          }
        },
        "border_JMAjFR": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "text_phgQQw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Taper candles hold a special place in home décor and <a href=\"https://www.lovetoknow.com/home/design-decor/what-is-taper-candle-adding-elegance-your-decor\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">ambiance creation</span></a>. We've compiled some frequently asked questions to help you make the most of Kisco's Bolsius candle collections.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-100"
          }
        },
        "spacer_mVH3Fw": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_jRWLhL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How Long Do Kisco's Taper Candles Typically Burn?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_cVFhCr": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Kisco's Bolsius taper candles come in long-burn options. The average burn time varies depending on the size of the candle but you cane find 6 hour, 8 hour , and even 12 hour burn taper candles here.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_iPXpEi": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_fVaWkq": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What taper candle height should I choose?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_xVMDY7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 10-inch and 11.5-inch tapers for formal tables, longer dinners, and taller candleholder styling, and choose 4-inch to 7-inch tapers when you want a lower profile or a shorter burn window. The assortment at Kisco Candles offers both classic dinner tapers and shorter household tapers, so you can match the candle to the scale of your setup.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_gbXCD9": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_63Jihh": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "How long do your taper candles burn?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_dttHE3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Burn time depends on the taper size and style. Our shorter Lerner tapers run from about 3 to 6 hours in the 4-inch to 7-inch range, and our longer classic tapers include 6-hour, 8-hour, and up to 12-hour options for extended use.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_fctQ8Y": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_YnWqLz": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Will these taper candles fit standard taper holders?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_HcQMNY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, most of our tapers have standard taper proportions that work with common candleholders. The collection includes classic 0.8-inch and 0.9-inch taper formats, so the cleanest fit usually comes from matching the base width to a holder made for standard dinner candles.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_XccrWr": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_GeeXti": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Are your taper candles dripless?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_XjKbnn": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, many choose our taper candles for a clean, low-mess burn. Just remember to place tapers upright in the correct holders and keep them away from drafts. For the best result, use a stable holder and keep the candles away from open windows, vents, and strong airflow.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_dzFcFC": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_bQqPgL": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which taper colors are best for weddings and formal tables?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_X8YXeg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>White and ivory are the safest starting points for weddings, dinner parties, and classic event décor. White gives you a crisp, bright finish, while ivory feels warmer and pairs especially well with cream florals, soft linens, and candlelit rooms.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_Jtnf8R": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 16
          }
        },
        "subheading_qF4bim": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What pack size should I buy for a small dinner versus a large event?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_9VhRC8": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose a 4-pack or 10-pack for home dining, styled photo shoots, or small gatherings, and move up to 30-pack, 45-pack, 50-pack, or 100-pack options when you are setting many tables or planning repeat use. We carry taper packs across several quantities so you can buy close to the number you actually need.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_f3hr7T": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_kiqgGx": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What is the difference between your classic dinner tapers and shorter household tapers?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_WPTEtt": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Classic dinner tapers are the better pick when you want a more formal, elongated look on the table. Shorter household tapers are useful when you want a lower flame line, a quicker burn, or a compact candle for smaller holders and tighter spaces.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_idYgNL": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_bUTgwQ": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Which taper candles work best for restaurants and hospitality spaces?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_7AHm7j": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Choose 7-inch to 10-inch tapers when you want an elegant look that still feels practical for dinner service. Those sizes give the table enough height to feel polished without making the candle harder to place, store, or replace between services.</p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "spacer_PLKAAd": {
          "type": "spacer",
          "settings": {
            "space": 12
          }
        },
        "subheading_YPM7Nt": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Can I mix taper sizes and colors in one order?",
            "subheading_tag": "h3",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-6-base"
          }
        },
        "text_4JwqeG": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Yes, you can build your order around the sizes and colors that fit your setup best. Many shoppers combine white or ivory long tapers for dining tables with shorter tapers for side tables, entry pieces, or secondary décor. </p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        }
      },
